From b513525ab90fd5fa2980361db0ee4fd0d0606ce6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:58:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] virtio/blk: add a hook called before each change to the
 disk

Let the embedder see every range the guest is about to change, before
the change, on the block worker's thread. A VMM that keeps checkpoints
of a running disk can then copy the old bytes of a range before they
are overwritten (copy-before-write), and keep a bitmap of the blocks
changed since the last checkpoint, without a second disk layer.

The hook is called before every write, write-zeroes and discard, with a
byte range already checked to lie inside the disk. Reads, flushes and
GET_ID do not call it. A hook that returns an error fails the request
with VIRTIO_BLK_S_IOERR and the disk is left as it was.

In Rust, `Block::set_write_hook` takes an `Arc<dyn BlockWriteHook>`. In
C, `krun_block_device_set_write_hook(handle, hook, user)` takes a
function `int32_t (*)(const void *user, uint64_t offset, uint64_t len)`
that returns 0 to let the change go on.

Assisted-by: Claude Code: claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
